  "goodToKnow": "Der Edelstahl is stainless steel, literally noble steel: eine Edelstahlspüle, Edelstahltöpfe. Strictly, Edelstahl means high-grade steel, and rostfreier Edelstahl is stainless. The town of Solingen is famous worldwide for its knives and blades, and Krupp in Essen developed stainless steel processes around 1912. Edel means noble: das Edelmetall, edel sei der Mensch (Goethe). It has no plural."
